  ('UAL-0023', 'E151', 'Brilliant Black BN; Black PN', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Liquorice • Black sweets • Desserts • Sauces', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Generally permitted within limits. As a synthetic azo colour, sensitivity reactions may occur in susceptible people.', '• Check for multiple artificial colours in dark sweets or desserts • Look for benzoates in coloured drinks/sauces', '• Colour-sensitive individuals • People prone to hives or allergies • Parents checking synthetic colours', 'Vegetable carbon • Cocoa • Caramelised ingredients', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Dark colour can hide several additives. Check whether the product is using one colour or building colour through a bigger additive stack.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0024', 'E153', 'Vegetable carbon', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Black sweets • Bakery decorations • Coatings • Specialist foods', 'Hours', 'Gut', 'Usually passes through; varies', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Vegetable carbon is generally considered low concern at permitted food-use levels. It is poorly absorbed.', '• Charcoal/carbon products can bind some substances; separate from medicines where advised • Check supplement use separately from food additive use', '• People taking regular medication should follow label/medical advice around charcoal products • People using activated charcoal supplements', 'Cocoa • Malt extract • Caramelised ingredients', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is a good example of context. As a colour in food it is different from taking charcoal supplements that are designed to bind substances.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0025', 'E155', 'Brown HT', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Chocolate desserts • Brown sauces • Sweets • Bakery decorations', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '1.5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Brown HT is a synthetic azo colour. Sensitivity reactions are possible in susceptible people and use is controlled by permitted limits.', '• Look for other synthetic colours in highly coloured products • Check total exposure from sweets, desserts and drinks', '• Colour-sensitive individuals • People prone to hives or allergies • Parents checking synthetic colours', 'Cocoa • Caramelised sugar • Malt extract', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'When a food is made strongly brown by additives rather than ingredients like cocoa, it is worth reading the full label.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0026', 'E160a', 'Carotenes', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Margarine and spreads • Cheese products • Desserts • Sauces', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', 'ADI varies by carotene source; see EFSA opinion', 'Carotenes are colour additives related to pigments found naturally in foods. Generally low concern within permitted food uses.', '• Also present naturally in foods and supplements • High-dose beta-carotene supplements are a separate consideration from normal food additive use', '• People taking high-dose beta-carotene supplements • Smokers/ex-smokers should be cautious with high-dose beta-carotene supplements', 'Carrot extract • Annatto • Turmeric', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Carotenes show why the source and dose matters. Food colouring levels are not the same as concentrated supplement use.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0027', 'E160c', 'Paprika extract; Capsanthian; Capsorubin', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Crisps and snacks • Sauces • Processed cheese • Meat-style products', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '24 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Paprika extract is a natural colour source. Sensitivity may occur in people sensitive to paprika or pepper-derived ingredients.', '• Often used in savoury snacks with salt, flavour enhancers and acidity regulators • Watch spicy seasoning blends if sensitive', '• People sensitive to paprika/chilli/pepper family ingredients • People prone to spice-related reflux or irritation', 'Paprika • Turmeric • Beta-carotene', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This can look more familiar than synthetic colours, but the whole product still matters, especially seasoned snacks.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0028', 'E160d', 'Lycopene', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Sauces • Soups • Spreads • Snacks', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '0.5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Lycopene is a red colour related to the natural pigment in tomatoes. Generally low concern within permitted food-use levels.', '• Also occurs naturally in tomato-based foods • Consider supplement intake separately from normal food additive exposure', '• People taking concentrated lycopene supplements', 'Tomato concentrate • Beetroot red • Paprika extract', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Lycopene is familiar from tomatoes. In the Unboxed view, the bigger question is whether it is in a simple food or a heavily processed product.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0029', 'E160e', 'Beta-apo-8''-carotenal (C30)', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Margarine and spreads • Cheese products • Desserts • Sauces', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '0.05 mg/kg body weight/day', 'A carotenoid colour used to create orange/red shades. Safety is based on permitted use levels and controlled intake.', '• Watch multiple carotenoid colours across the day • Supplements are a separate exposure route from food additive use', '• People taking high-dose carotenoid supplements • People wanting to minimise synthetic/isolated colours', 'Beta-carotene • Paprika extract • Annatto', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is one to recognise because it sounds less familiar than beta-carotene, even though it sits in the carotenoid colour family.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0030', 'E161b', 'Lutein', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Egg products • Sauces • Desserts • Dairy-style products', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '1 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Lutein is a carotenoid colour also found naturally in foods such as leafy greens and egg yolk. Generally low concern within permitted food uses.', '• Also found in supplements marketed for eye health • Consider total intake if using high-dose supplements', '• People taking concentrated lutein supplements', 'Marigold extract • Egg yolk colour • Beta-carotene', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Lutein is another additive where normal food-use context is very different from concentrated supplement doses.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0031', 'E161g', 'Canthaxanthin', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Specialist foods • Animal-product colour uses • Limited food applications', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', 'Several days / varies', '0.03 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Canthaxanthin has a low ADI and is more tightly controlled than many colours. High intakes from non-food/supplement sources have been linked with eye-related deposits.', '• Avoid stacking with canthaxanthin-containing supplements/tanning products • Watch repeated exposure from specialist products', '• People using tanning or carotenoid supplements • People with eye health concerns • High-frequency consumers of products using this colour', 'Paprika extract • Beta-carotene • Lycopene', 'Approved with controlled permitted uses and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is not a common everyday label check for most families, but the low ADI makes it one to log accurately in the database.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0032', 'E162', 'Beetroot Red; Betanin', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Yoghurts • Ice cream • Sweets • Desserts', 'Hours', 'Gut • Kidneys', '24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Beetroot red/betanin is generally considered low concern at permitted food-use levels. Colour can be affected by heat and acidity.', '• Often found in red/pink foods alongside acids such as citric acid • Check total sugar and sweetener load in coloured desserts', '• People sensitive to beetroot ingredients • People monitoring oxalate intake should consider overall diet, not just additive use', 'Beetroot juice • Anthocyanins • Paprika extract', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is one of the more recognisable natural colours. Still, a naturally derived colour does not automatically make the whole product simple.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0033', 'E163', 'Anthocyanins', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Drinks • Desserts • Jams • Sweets', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver', '24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Anthocyanins are plant pigments found in fruits and vegetables. Generally low concern within permitted food-use levels.', '• Colour changes with acidity, so often found with citric acid or other acids • Watch sugar, acids and sweeteners in brightly coloured drinks', '• People sensitive to specific fruit/plant sources used • People with allergy concerns should check source ingredients where listed', 'Fruit/berry concentrates • Beetroot red • Paprika extract', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Anthocyanins are familiar plant pigments, but Unboxed still looks at the whole label: colour, acid, sweetener and preservative together.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0034', 'E170', 'Calcium carbonate', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Fortified foods • Bakery products • Chewing gum • Confectionery', 'Hours', 'Gut', 'Varies', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Calcium carbonate is commonly used as a colour, acidity regulator or calcium source. Generally low concern at permitted food-use levels.', '• Also present in supplements and antacids • Consider total calcium intake if using high-dose supplements', '• People taking high-dose calcium supplements • People with kidney stone history should follow medical advice on calcium intake', 'Calcium-rich ingredients • Rice flour • Starch-based colours', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is another E number that can also be a mineral source. The issue is not the name alone, but the dose and product context.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0035', 'E171', 'Titanium dioxide', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🔴 Highest Awareness', '5/5', '• White sweets/decorations • Chewing gum • White sauces/coatings • Some food supplements', 'Varies', 'Poorly absorbed; particles may persist', 'Varies / may persist', 'ADI not established; EFSA could not confirm safety as a food additive', 'EFSA concluded E171 could no longer be considered safe as a food additive because genotoxicity concerns could not be ruled out. UK position differs between GB and Northern Ireland.', '• Look for white colouring in sweets, icing, decorations and supplements • Check GB vs NI/EU regulatory status • Consider non-food exposure separately', '• Parents checking sweets/decorations • People wanting to avoid additives with unresolved genotoxicity questions • Supplement users', 'Calcium carbonate • Rice starch • Starch-based opacifiers', 'Great Britain: authorised. Northern Ireland/EU: not permitted for food additive use following EU rules.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; COT', 'This is one of the clearest examples of why UK-specific status matters. It is allowed in Great Britain but not in Northern Ireland/EU food use.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://cot.food.gov.uk/COT%20Evaluations', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/news/titanium-dioxide-e171-no-longer-considered-safe-when-used-food-additive', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added with GB/NI divergence. EFSA and UK COT positions should be kept under review.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0036', 'E172', 'Iron oxides and hydroxides', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Confectionery • Bakery decorations • Coatings • Specialist foods', 'Hours', 'Gut', 'Varies', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Iron oxides and hydroxides are mineral colour additives. Generally low concern at permitted food-use levels.', '• Also used in non-food products; food-grade permitted use differs from cosmetic/industrial use • Watch decorative foods with multiple colours/coatings', '• People advised to monitor iron exposure should consider total dietary and supplement intake • People avoiding decorative additives', 'Cocoa • Fruit/veg powders • Caramelised ingredients', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Mineral colours can sound industrial, but the food-grade context and permitted limits are what matter. Still check decorative foods carefully.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0037', 'E173', 'Aluminium', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Cake decorations • Confectionery coatings • Specialist decorative foods', 'Varies', 'Poorly absorbed; excretion varies', 'Varies', 'Based on aluminium tolerable weekly intake; see EFSA opinion', 'Aluminium as a colour has limited uses. Aluminium exposure is assessed across diet and other sources, not just one additive.', '• Watch decorative products that use metallic colours • Consider total aluminium exposure from other food additives and sources', '• Children with high intake of decorative products • People advised to limit aluminium exposure • People with kidney disease should follow medical advice', 'Mica-based decorations where permitted • Fruit/veg colours • Cocoa', 'Approved for specific permitted uses and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Metallic-looking food decoration is the clue. This is less about everyday meals and more about special decorative products and total exposure.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0038', 'E174', 'Silver', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cake decorations • Confectionery coatings • Specialist decorative foods', 'Varies', 'Poorly absorbed', 'Varies', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Silver is used as a decorative colour in limited food applications. Intake is controlled through permitted uses and limits.', '• Watch edible metallic decorations • Avoid assuming decorative products are everyday foods', '• Children consuming decorative sweets/cakes frequently • People wanting to minimise metallic colour additives', 'Fruit/veg colours • Cocoa • Non-metallic decorations', 'Approved for specific permitted uses and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Silver is mainly a decoration issue. Unboxed would treat it as a label check for novelty foods, not a normal daily food ingredient.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0039', 'E175', 'Gold', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cake decorations • Confectionery coatings • Specialist decorative foods', 'Varies', 'Poorly absorbed', 'Varies', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Gold is used as a decorative colour in limited food applications. Intake is controlled through permitted uses and limits.', '• Watch edible metallic decorations • Avoid regular use of novelty/decorative foods as everyday snacks', '• Children consuming decorative sweets/cakes frequently • People wanting to minimise metallic colour additives', 'Fruit/veg colours • Cocoa • Non-metallic decorations', 'Approved for specific permitted uses and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Gold looks premium, but it is still an additive. It belongs in occasional decorative food rather than everyday intake.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0040', 'E180', 'Litholrubine BK', 'Colours', 'Colouring', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Edible cheese rinds • Specialist rind-coloured cheeses', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '1.5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Litholrubine BK is a synthetic colour with restricted food uses, notably edible cheese rind. Sensitivity reactions may occur in susceptible people.', '• Mostly relevant to rind-coloured cheeses • Check if the rind is intended to be eaten', '• Colour-sensitive individuals • People prone to hives or allergies • People who regularly eat coloured cheese rinds', 'Annatto • Paprika extract • Natural rind colouring approaches', 'Approved for specific limited uses and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is not a common additive across lots of foods, but it matters when the coloured rind is eaten.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0041', 'E200', 'Sorbic acid', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cheese • Cakes • Sauces • Dips', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '25 mg/kg body weight/day as sorbic acid', 'Sorbic acid is a preservative used to inhibit moulds and yeasts. Generally well tolerated, though skin or gut sensitivity can occur in some people.', '• Often appears with other preservatives in long-life foods • Watch repeated exposure from sauces, dips, bakery and dairy-style products', '• People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to skin or gut reactions', 'Vinegar • Fermentation • Refrigeration • Shorter shelf-life recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is a shelf-life additive. The Unboxed question is how often your food needs preserving to last longer than real food normally would.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0042', 'E202', 'Potassium sorbate', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cheese • Cakes • Sauces • Dips', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', '24–48 hrs*', '25 mg/kg body weight/day as sorbic acid', 'Potassium sorbate is a sorbate preservative used to inhibit moulds and yeasts. Generally well tolerated, but sensitivity can occur in some people.', '• Often appears with acids and other preservatives • Check long-life dips, sauces, bakery fillings and dairy-style products', '• People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to skin or gut reactions', 'Vinegar • Fermentation • Refrigeration • Shorter shelf-life recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'A useful label clue: if a product needs potassium sorbate, it has probably been designed for shelf life as much as nourishment.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Detail added for Unboxed Additive Library v1.0. Timeline is practical guidance, not a guaranteed individual clearance time.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0043', 'E210', 'Benzoic acid', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Soft drinks and squash • Sauces and dressings • Pickles and condiments • Fruit-based products', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0–5 mg/kg body weight/day as benzoic acid (group ADI)', 'Benzoates are rapidly absorbed and excreted. EFSA kept the group ADI but noted high consumers, especially toddlers and children consuming flavoured drinks regularly, can exceed it in some scenarios.', '• Watch soft drinks, squash and acidic sauces • Sodium/potassium/calcium benzoates count towards the same group ADI • In acidic drinks, benzoates need careful formulation when vitamin C/ascorbic acid is present', '• Young children with frequent soft drink intake • People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to hives or allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Pasteurisation • Fermentation • Vinegar/lemon in fresh recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Benzoic acid is part of the benzoate family. The Unboxed check is not one label line alone, but how often benzoates show up across drinks and sauces in the same day.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4433', '2026-07-05', 'Benzoate group entry. ADI and exposure summary from EFSA 2016. Benzene wording kept cautious: formulation issue in acidic drinks, not a direct claim for every product.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0044', 'E211', 'Sodium benzoate', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Fizzy drinks • Squash • Sauces • Pickles and condiments', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0–5 mg/kg body weight/day as benzoic acid (group ADI)', 'Benzoates are rapidly absorbed and excreted. EFSA kept the group ADI but noted high consumers, especially toddlers and children consuming flavoured drinks regularly, can exceed it in some scenarios.', '• Watch soft drinks, squash and acidic sauces • Sodium/potassium/calcium benzoates count towards the same group ADI • In acidic drinks, benzoates need careful formulation when vitamin C/ascorbic acid is present', '• Young children with frequent soft drink intake • People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to hives or allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Pasteurisation • Fermentation • Vinegar/lemon in fresh recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Sodium benzoate is one of the preservatives worth learning because it appears in everyday drinks and sauces. Check the full day, especially for children.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4433', '2026-07-05', 'Benzoate group entry. ADI and exposure summary from EFSA 2016. Benzene wording kept cautious: formulation issue in acidic drinks, not a direct claim for every product.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0045', 'E212', 'Potassium benzoate', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Soft drinks and squash • Sauces and dressings • Pickles and condiments • Fruit-based products', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0–5 mg/kg body weight/day as benzoic acid (group ADI)', 'Benzoates are rapidly absorbed and excreted. EFSA kept the group ADI but noted high consumers, especially toddlers and children consuming flavoured drinks regularly, can exceed it in some scenarios.', '• Watch soft drinks, squash and acidic sauces • Sodium/potassium/calcium benzoates count towards the same group ADI • In acidic drinks, benzoates need careful formulation when vitamin C/ascorbic acid is present', '• Young children with frequent soft drink intake • People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to hives or allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Pasteurisation • Fermentation • Vinegar/lemon in fresh recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Potassium benzoate works like other benzoates. Different salt, same family, so the daily total matters more than the exact version.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4433', '2026-07-05', 'Benzoate group entry. ADI and exposure summary from EFSA 2016. Benzene wording kept cautious: formulation issue in acidic drinks, not a direct claim for every product.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0046', 'E213', 'Calcium benzoate', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Sauces • Pickles • Fruit products • Specialist preserved foods', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0–5 mg/kg body weight/day as benzoic acid (group ADI)', 'Benzoates are rapidly absorbed and excreted. EFSA kept the group ADI but noted high consumers, especially toddlers and children consuming flavoured drinks regularly, can exceed it in some scenarios.', '• Watch soft drinks, squash and acidic sauces • Sodium/potassium/calcium benzoates count towards the same group ADI • In acidic drinks, benzoates need careful formulation when vitamin C/ascorbic acid is present', '• Young children with frequent soft drink intake • People with preservative sensitivity • People prone to hives or allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Pasteurisation • Fermentation • Vinegar/lemon in fresh recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Calcium benzoate is another form of the same preservative family. Treat it as part of your total benzoate exposure.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4433', '2026-07-05', 'Benzoate group entry. ADI and exposure summary from EFSA 2016. Benzene wording kept cautious: formulation issue in acidic drinks, not a direct claim for every product.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0047', 'E214', 'Ethyl p-hydroxybenzoate', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Sauces • Pickles • Confectionery coatings • Specialist preserved foods', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0–10 mg/kg body weight/day as the sum of methyl and ethyl parabens and their sodium salts (group ADI)', 'EFSA established a group ADI for methyl and ethyl parabens and their sodium salts. Parabens preserve against yeasts and moulds; sensitivity reactions are possible in some people.', '• Counts with other methyl/ethyl paraben preservatives • Check long shelf-life sauces, coatings and specialist products • Do not assume cosmetic paraben debates apply directly to food exposure levels', '• People with preservative sensitivity • People with known paraben allergy • People prone to hives or allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Fermentation • Vinegar • Shorter shelf-life recipes', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Ethyl paraben is not as familiar as benzoates or sulphites, but it is still a shelf-life preservative. Look for it in products designed to last.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging/Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/news/efsa-advises-safety-paraben-usage-food', '2026-07-05', 'Paraben group. EFSA 2004 supports group ADI for methyl/ethyl parabens and salts; propyl paraben excluded from group ADI and is not in this UK list batch.', TRUE),
