  ('UAL-0051', 'E220', 'Sulphur dioxide', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative / antioxidant', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Dried fruit • Wine and cider • Bottled drinks • Prepared potato products', 'Minutes to hours', 'Liver • Enzymes', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0.7 mg SO2 equivalent/kg body weight/day (temporary group ADI used in EFSA assessment)', 'Sulphites can trigger sensitivity reactions in susceptible people, including asthma-like symptoms. EFSA has identified exposure concerns for some population groups and continues to review the evidence base.', '• All sulphites E220–E228 count together as SO2 equivalents • Look out for dried fruit, wine/cider, bottled drinks and prepared potato products • Alcohol plus sulphites may make reactions more noticeable in sensitive people', '• People with sulphite sensitivity • People with asthma • Children with frequent dried fruit/juice intake • People prone to allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Freezing • Fermentation control • Fresh preparation • Ascorbic acid in some uses', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels. Sulphites above labelling thresholds must be declared as an allergen-style ingredient.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Sulphur dioxide is a big one for sensitive people. It is not about panic; it is about spotting whether sulphites are repeatedly appearing in drinks, dried fruit and prepared foods.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4438', '2026-07-05', 'Sulphite group entry. EFSA 2016 temporary group ADI and 2025 exposure update noted. Keep language focused on susceptible groups and cumulative SO2-equivalent exposure.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0052', 'E221', 'Sodium sulphite', 'Preservatives', 'Preservative / antioxidant', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Dried fruit • Wine and cider • Bottled drinks • Prepared potato products', 'Minutes to hours', 'Liver • Enzymes', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '0.7 mg SO2 equivalent/kg body weight/day (temporary group ADI used in EFSA assessment)', 'Sulphites can trigger sensitivity reactions in susceptible people, including asthma-like symptoms. EFSA has identified exposure concerns for some population groups and continues to review the evidence base.', '• All sulphites E220–E228 count together as SO2 equivalents • Look out for dried fruit, wine/cider, bottled drinks and prepared potato products • Alcohol plus sulphites may make reactions more noticeable in sensitive people', '• People with sulphite sensitivity • People with asthma • Children with frequent dried fruit/juice intake • People prone to allergy-type reactions', 'Refrigeration • Freezing • Fermentation control • Fresh preparation • Ascorbic acid in some uses', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and maximum levels. Sulphites above labelling thresholds must be declared as an allergen-style ingredient.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Sodium sulphite belongs to the same sulphite family. If you react to one sulphite, the whole E220–E228 group is worth checking.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2016.4438', '2026-07-05', 'Sulphite group entry. EFSA 2016 temporary group ADI and 2025 exposure update noted. Keep language focused on susceptible groups and cumulative SO2-equivalent exposure.', TRUE),
