  ('UAL-0176', 'E1103', 'Invertase', 'Emulsifiers, stabilisers, thickeners and gelling agents', 'Enzyme / sugar texture modifier', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Fondant fillings • Soft-centred chocolates • Confectionery • Bakery fillings', 'Hours', 'Digestion • Gut', 'Digested like protein / varies*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Invertase is an enzyme used to break sucrose into glucose and fructose, helping create soft centres in confectionery.', '• Main concern is usually the sugar/confectionery context • Not an emulsifier risk like E471/E472 • Check allergen/manufacturing information if enzyme source matters', '• People reducing sugar/confectionery • People with specific enzyme/allergen concerns • Parents reviewing sweets for children', 'Traditional confectionery methods • Lower-sugar recipes • Simpler fillings', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Invertase is mainly a confectionery tool. The additive itself is usually less important than the sugar-heavy food it appears in.', '⭐⭐⭐ Limited / functional enzyme', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0177', 'E260', 'Acetic acid', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator / preservative support', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Pickles • Sauces • Dressings • Chutneys • Bakery products', 'Hours', 'Liver • Energy metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Acetic acid is the main acid in vinegar and is used to adjust acidity and support preservation. EFSA found no safety concern at authorised uses.', '• Acid load may matter for teeth/reflux in some people • Often appears in preserved sauces/pickles • Check salt and sugar in the same product', '• People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People monitoring dental enamel exposure • People eating acidic sauces frequently', 'Vinegar • Lemon juice • Fermentation-derived acids', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is basically the vinegar acid. For most people it is low concern; the product around it often matters more.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2020.6032', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0178', 'E261', 'Potassium acetate', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator / preservative support', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Sauces • Pickled products • Bakery products • Processed foods where permitted', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Potassium acetate is an acetate salt used to control acidity and support preservation. It is related to acetic acid chemistry.', '• Adds potassium, usually small amounts • Check with acidic/preserved foods • Product salt/sugar profile may matter more', '• People on potassium-restricted medical diets • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People tracking preserved foods', 'Vinegar • Fermentation • Shorter shelf-life recipes', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is a low-awareness acidity additive for most people. It tells you the product has been adjusted for stability and shelf life.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.2903/j.efsa.2020.6032', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
