  ('UAL-0182', 'E290', 'Carbon dioxide', 'Others', 'Packaging gas / propellant / carbonation', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Fizzy drinks • Packaged foods • Modified atmosphere packaging • Whipped products', 'Minutes to hours', 'Breathing • Blood buffering', 'Cleared rapidly via lungs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Carbon dioxide is used for carbonation and packaging atmosphere. It is normally cleared rapidly through breathing.', '• In drinks, acidity and sugar/sweeteners matter more • Carbonation may worsen bloating/reflux for some • Not a chemical-residue concern for most people', '• People with reflux or bloating • People reducing fizzy drinks • Children with high soft drink intake', 'Still drinks • Fresh packaging • Non-carbonated options', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Carbon dioxide itself is low concern. In fizzy drinks, the bigger issues are acids, sweeteners, caffeine and sugar.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
