  ('UAL-0196', 'E338', 'Phosphoric acid', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Cola drinks • Soft drinks • Processed foods • Flavourings where permitted', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Phosphoric acid is part of the phosphate additive group. EFSA established a group ADI expressed as phosphorus and noted exposure can be high in some population groups.', '• Common cola acid • Adds to total phosphate load • Watch with processed meat, processed cheese and other phosphate additives', '• Children drinking cola often • People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • People tracking bone/mineral balance', 'Citric acid in some formulations • Lower-phosphate drinks • Water/milk as appropriate', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Phosphoric acid is one of the additives worth recognising in cola. The issue is total phosphate load across the diet.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0197', 'E339', 'Sodium phosphates', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator / stabiliser / emulsifying salt', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Processed cheese • Processed meat • Bakery products • Desserts • Ready meals', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Sodium phosphates are part of the phosphate additive group. EFSA set a group ADI and highlighted total phosphate exposure as relevant.', '• Adds sodium and phosphate load • Often used with other phosphates • Check processed cheese/meat and ready meals', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • People tracking sodium intake • Children eating many processed foods', 'Traditional cheese/meat processing • Citrates where suitable • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Sodium phosphates are a big processed-food marker. They are not just texture; they add to the phosphate load across the day.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0198', 'E340', 'Potassium phosphates', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator / stabiliser', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Processed meat • Processed cheese • Drinks • Desserts • Ready meals', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Potassium phosphates are part of the phosphate additive group. EFSA set a group ADI expressed as phosphorus.', '• Adds phosphate and potassium load • Watch with multiple phosphate additives • Relevant in processed meat/cheese/ready meals', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • People on potassium-restricted medical diets • Children eating many processed foods', 'Fresh preparation • Non-phosphate processing methods • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is in the phosphate awareness group. The product can look normal, but phosphates can stack across the day.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0199', 'E341', 'Calcium phosphates', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator / anti-caking / raising agent', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Flour products • Bakery mixes • Supplements/fortified foods • Desserts • Powdered foods', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Calcium phosphates are part of the phosphate additive group. They can function as acidity regulators, anti-caking agents or raising agents.', '• Adds phosphate load • May appear in fortified/powdered foods • Check with other phosphates and supplements', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • People using mineral supplements • Children eating many fortified/processed foods', 'Calcium carbonate where suitable • Traditional baking methods • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Calcium phosphate can sound like a nutrient, but as an additive it still contributes to total phosphate exposure.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0200', 'E343', 'Magnesium phosphates', 'Others', 'Anti-caking / acidity regulator', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Powdered foods • Supplements • Bakery mixes • Processed foods where permitted', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Magnesium phosphates are included in the phosphate additive group re-evaluated by EFSA. Total phosphate exposure is the key consideration.', '• Adds phosphate load • Often appears in powders/supplements • Check with other phosphate additives', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • People using multiple supplements • People tracking mineral additives', 'Magnesium salts without phosphate where suitable • Better powder storage • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Another phosphate additive. The Unboxed question is how many phosphate sources are showing up across the full day.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0201', 'E350', 'Sodium malates', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Sweets • Drinks • Desserts • Fruit-flavoured products • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Energy metabolism • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / re-evaluation data call noted', 'Sodium malates are salts of malic acid used to regulate acidity. EFSA has requested data for malic acid and malates re-evaluation.', '• Acid load matters in sweets/drinks • Adds sodium, usually modestly • Watch with citric/malic/fumaric acid stacks', '• People tracking sodium intake • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • Children eating sour sweets/drinks often', 'Fruit acids • Lemon/lime juice • Lower-acid formulations', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Sodium malates are part of the sour/acidic product picture. The stack is usually more important than one salt.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging / re-evaluation pending', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/food-improvement-agents/additives/re-evaluation_en', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0202', 'E351', 'Potassium malate', 'Others', 'Acidity regulator', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Sweets • Drinks • Desserts • Fruit-flavoured products • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Energy metabolism • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / re-evaluation data call noted', 'Potassium malate is a malic acid salt used to regulate acidity and flavour sharpness. EFSA has requested data for the malate group.', '• Acid load matters in sour products • Adds potassium, usually modestly • Watch with other acids and sweeteners', '• People on potassium-restricted medical diets • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • Children eating sour sweets/drinks often', 'Fruit acids • Lemon/lime juice • Lower-acid recipes', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Potassium malate is another acidity regulator. For Unboxed, the key is repeated sour drink and sweet exposure.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging / re-evaluation pending', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/food-improvement-agents/additives/re-evaluation_en', '2026-07-07', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Use additive-specific toxicokinetic evidence where available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0203', 'E352', 'Calcium malates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Sweets • Drinks • Desserts • Fruit-flavoured products • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Energy metabolism • Calcium/mineral balance', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / re-evaluation data call noted', 'Calcium malates are salts of malic acid used mainly to regulate acidity. At approved food-use levels they are generally expected to be low concern, but additive-specific re-evaluation detail remains limited.', '• Acid load matters in sour sweets/drinks • Adds calcium, usually modestly • Watch alongside other acidity regulators', '• People with reflux/acid sensitivity • Children consuming many sour sweets/drinks • People tracking mineral supplements', 'Fruit acids • Lemon/lime juice • Lower-acid formulations', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA re-evaluation programme', 'Calcium malates are not a headline additive, but they sit in the sour/acidic product stack. The bigger Unboxed issue is repeated acidic processed snacks and drinks.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging / re-evaluation pending', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/food-improvement-agents/additives/re-evaluation_en', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0204', 'E353', 'Metatartaric acid', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Wine • Fermented drinks • Products where tartaric stability is needed', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / use-specific exposure expected to be low', 'Metatartaric acid is used mainly as a stabiliser, especially to reduce tartrate crystal formation in wine. Normal food-use exposure is generally low.', '• Mostly relevant in wine/drink exposure • Alcohol itself is usually the larger risk driver • Counts with other acidity regulators', '• People avoiding alcohol • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People sensitive to wine additives', 'Cold stabilisation • Minimal additive winemaking where suitable', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'This is more of a processing/stability additive than a daily food-stack concern. In wine, the wider alcohol and sulphite context usually matters more.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging / limited additive-specific detail', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0205', 'E354', 'Calcium tartrate', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Bakery products • Desserts • Sweets • Wine-related products • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '240 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI as tartaric acid for E334-E337 and E354', 'Calcium tartrate is part of the tartrate additive group. EFSA set a group ADI expressed as tartaric acid, with typical food-use exposure generally not a concern for most people.', '• Counts within tartrate group exposure • Adds calcium, usually modestly • Watch with other acidity regulators', '• People with reflux/acid sensitivity • Children consuming many sweets/bakery products • People with medically restricted diets', 'Cream of tartar-style ingredients • Lemon juice • Traditional baking methods', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Calcium tartrate is usually low concern on its own. The Unboxed check is whether it appears inside a bigger sweet/bakery additive stack.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/6030', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0206', 'E355', 'Adipic acid', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Desserts • Powdered desserts • Jelly-type products • Bakery mixes • Drinks where permitted', 'Hours', 'Gut • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '0-5 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI for adipic acid and adipates', 'Adipic acid is an acidity regulator. Approved exposure is controlled by permitted uses and limits, but it is a synthetic acidulant and may contribute to sour/acid load in processed products.', '• Sour/acid product stacking • May appear with colours, sweeteners and preservatives • Consider total intake from drinks/sweets/desserts', '• Children consuming many sweets/drinks • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People sensitive to acidic processed foods', 'Citric fruit acids • Lemon/lime juice • Less acidic recipes', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA/JECFA-style ADI references', 'This is not one of the most recognised additives, but it often belongs to the same sour processed-food pattern: flavour hit, colour, sweetener and acid together.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate / older ADI basis', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0207', 'E356', 'Sodium adipate', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Desserts • Powdered desserts • Bakery mixes • Drinks where permitted • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Kidneys • Sodium balance', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '0-5 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI for adipic acid and adipates', 'Sodium adipate is a salt of adipic acid used for acidity control. Main awareness points are acidulant stacking and small additional sodium contribution.', '• Adds to adipate group exposure • Adds sodium, usually modestly • Often appears in processed dessert/drink-style products', '• People tracking sodium intake • Children consuming many processed sweets/drinks • People with reflux/acid sensitivity', 'Citric fruit acids • Lower-sodium formulations • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA/JECFA-style ADI references', 'Sodium adipate is usually not a stand-alone problem. It becomes more relevant when it is part of a processed product built around acids, colours and sweeteners.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate / older ADI basis', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0208', 'E357', 'Potassium adipate', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Desserts • Powdered desserts • Drinks where permitted • Bakery mixes • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Kidneys • Potassium balance', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '0-5 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI for adipic acid and adipates', 'Potassium adipate is an adipic acid salt used as an acidity regulator. Typical exposure is controlled, but it still adds to the synthetic acidulant pattern in processed products.', '• Adds to adipate group exposure • Adds potassium, usually modestly • Watch with sour product stacks', '• People on potassium-restricted medical diets • People with reflux/acid sensitivity • Children consuming many sweets/drinks', 'Citric fruit acids • Lower-acid formulations • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA/JECFA-style ADI references', 'Potassium adipate is a moderate awareness additive because context matters: product type, acid load and repeated exposure across the day.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate / older ADI basis', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0209', 'E363', 'Succinic acid', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Desserts • Soups/sauces • Drinks • Seasonings • Processed foods where permitted', 'Hours', 'Energy metabolism • Gut', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated in routine guidance', 'Succinic acid occurs naturally in metabolism and some foods. As an additive it is used for acidity/flavour balance and is generally low concern at normal food-use levels.', '• Acid/flavour stacking in savoury or sour products • May appear with flavour enhancers or preservatives • Product context matters more than the single additive', '• People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People sensitive to strong savoury/sour processed foods', 'Fermentation acids • Vinegar/lemon where suitable • Simpler seasoning', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'Succinic acid is not a major red flag by itself. The Unboxed lens is whether it is part of a heavily engineered flavour profile.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0210', 'E380', 'Triammonium citrate', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Drinks • Desserts • Processed cheese-style products • Sauces • Foods needing acidity buffering', 'Hours', 'Liver • Kidneys', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not limited for citrates in general food-use context', 'Triammonium citrate is a citrate salt used for acidity buffering and stability. Citrates are generally low concern at approved food-use levels, though product context still matters.', '• Citrate/acidity regulator stacking • May appear with phosphates or emulsifying salts • Ammonium contribution is normally small at permitted levels', '• People with reflux/acid sensitivity • People with medically restricted diets • Children consuming many processed drinks/desserts', 'Lemon juice • Citric acid from fruit sources • Simpler processing', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'This is usually a low-drama stabiliser/acidity regulator. The better question is why the product needs that level of buffering in the first place.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0211', 'E385', 'Calcium disodium ethylene diamine tetra-acetate; calcium disodium EDTA', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Canned foods • Sauces/dressings • Pulses/beans • Shellfish/fish products • Preserved foods where permitted', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral binding', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '1.9 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as EDTA', 'Calcium disodium EDTA is a sequestrant that binds metal ions to protect colour/flavour and reduce oxidation. EFSA established an ADI; awareness is higher because the additive works by mineral/metal chelation.', '• Can appear in preserved foods • Watch with low-mineral diets or repeated processed-food intake • Product stack may include preservatives, acids and salt', '• Children with high processed-food intake • People with kidney disease should seek clinical advice • People with mineral deficiency concerns', 'Fresh foods • Glass-packed foods without sequestrants • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'EDTA is one of the additives worth recognising. Its job is to bind metals, which is useful for shelf life, but repeated exposure deserves more awareness.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5361', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0212', 'E422', 'Glycerol', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cakes • Icings • Sweets • Low-fat foods • Dried fruit • Drinks', 'Hours', 'Liver • Gut', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'Glycerol is used as a humectant, solvent and sweet-tasting carrier. It is generally low concern at normal food additive levels, but higher intakes can have laxative or digestive effects.', '• Humectant load in sweets/bars • May appear with sweeteners and polyols • Check serving size in high-moisture snacks', '• People with IBS or sensitive digestion • Children eating lots of sweets • People tracking sugar alcohol/polyol-style effects', 'Honey/syrup in traditional recipes • Moisture control through fresh preparation', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'Glycerol is often more about texture and moisture than danger. The Unboxed check is repeated intake from sweets, bars and ultra-processed snacks.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0213', 'E423', 'Octenyl succinic acid modified gum Arabic', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Emulsified drinks • Flavour preparations • Sauces • Dressings • Foods needing stable flavour/oil dispersion', 'Hours to days', 'Gut • Immune sensitivity', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / evaluated within modified gum context', 'Octenyl succinic acid modified gum Arabic is used as an emulsifier/stabiliser, especially for flavour oils. Gum Arabic is generally well tolerated, but modification and emulsifier exposure make this a moderate-awareness entry.', '• Emulsifier stack with other gums/stabilisers • Often used in flavour systems • Check repeated exposure in drinks and sauces', '• People with sensitive digestion • People reacting to gums/emulsifiers • Children consuming many flavoured drinks', 'Plain gum Arabic where suitable • Lecithin or simpler emulsification • Fresh mixing', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'This is a more technical emulsifier. It is not automatically high risk, but it belongs in the gut/emulsifier awareness group.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate / limited public detail', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0214', 'E450', 'Diphosphates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Processed cheese • Processed meat • Bakery products • Desserts • Ready meals • Powdered products', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Diphosphates are part of the phosphate additive group. EFSA set a group ADI expressed as phosphorus, and phosphate additives are more bioavailable than naturally bound phosphorus in whole foods.', '• Adds to total phosphate load • Often combined with other phosphates • Common in processed meat/cheese/bakery stacks', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • Children with high processed-food intake • People eating frequent processed meat/cheese products', 'Traditional processing • Fresh meat/cheese • Non-phosphate raising systems where possible', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Diphosphates are a key Unboxed awareness additive. They can make processed food perform better, but also add to the hidden phosphate load.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0215', 'E451', 'Triphosphates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Processed meat • Processed cheese • Ready meals • Seafood products • Bakery/powdered mixes', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Triphosphates are part of the phosphate additive group and contribute to total dietary phosphate exposure. EFSA identified phosphate additives as a group needing clear intake management.', '• Adds to phosphate load • Often used with other phosphates • May improve water retention/texture in processed foods', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • Children with high processed-food intake • People eating frequent processed meat/seafood', 'Fresh products • Traditional processing • Shorter ingredient lists', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Triphosphates are not just a technical texture additive. They are part of the wider phosphate-load picture across processed foods.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0216', 'E452', 'Polyphosphates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Processed meat • Processed cheese • Seafood products • Ready meals • Powdered foods', 'Hours', 'Kidneys • Mineral balance', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '40 mg/kg body weight/day group ADI expressed as phosphorus for phosphates', 'Polyphosphates are part of the phosphate additive group. They are used for water binding, texture and stability, and can contribute meaningfully to phosphate exposure in processed diets.', '• High relevance in processed meat/seafood • Adds to group phosphate exposure • Watch with other phosphate additives in the same day', '• People with kidney disease or phosphate restrictions • Children eating frequent ultra-processed foods • People eating processed meat/seafood often', 'Fresh meat/fish • Traditional preparation • Non-phosphate stabilisation where possible', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Polyphosphates are a major Unboxed flag because they are often invisible to consumers but can change both product texture and phosphate exposure.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/5674', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0217', 'E459', 'Beta-cyclodextrin', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Flavour encapsulation • Tablet-style foods/supplements • Chewing gum • Foods needing carrier technology where permitted', 'Hours', 'Gut • Absorption/carrier effects', 'Usually within 24-48 hrs*', '5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'Beta-cyclodextrin is a cyclic carbohydrate used to carry, encapsulate or stabilise compounds. EFSA has assessed it with an ADI; awareness is moderate because it can alter delivery of flavours or other substances.', '• Carrier/encapsulation use can hide formulation complexity • Watch with supplements and fortified products • Not usually a broad everyday exposure additive', '• People with sensitive digestion • Children consuming many fortified/technical products • People using multiple supplements', 'Simpler flavour systems • Less encapsulated ingredients • Fresh flavour sources', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is a technical additive. It is not a classic colour/preservative issue, but it shows how modern foods can be engineered at delivery-system level.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate/strong', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/efsajournal/pub/4628', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0218', 'E499', 'Stigmasterol-rich plant sterols', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Fortified foods • Spreads/drinks with plant sterols • Cholesterol-lowering food products where permitted', 'Hours to days', 'Liver • Cholesterol metabolism • Fat-soluble nutrients', 'Variable; effect relates to repeated intake*', 'ADI not specified / use controlled by permitted food categories and labelling', 'Stigmasterol-rich plant sterols are used in specific foods to help reduce cholesterol absorption. They can also reduce absorption of some carotenoids, so use is targeted rather than general-purpose.', '• Works through repeated intake • Consider total plant sterol exposure • Product may be unsuitable for groups not needing cholesterol lowering', '• People not advised to lower cholesterol • Pregnant/breastfeeding people and young children unless advised • People on cholesterol medication should check advice', 'Whole-food fibre • Oats/barley beta-glucans • Nuts/seeds • Diet/lifestyle support', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels with specific labelling requirements for plant sterol foods.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'This is a functional additive, not just a processing aid. It should be used knowingly, not accidentally as part of a normal snack pattern.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0219', 'E500', 'Sodium carbonates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Baking powder • Biscuits/cakes • Cocoa products • Noodles • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Sodium balance', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not limited in normal food-use context', 'Sodium carbonates are alkalising agents and raising agents. They are generally low concern at approved levels, though they add sodium and can affect digestive comfort in some products.', '• Adds sodium • Common in bakery/raising systems • Watch with salty processed-food stacks', '• People tracking sodium intake • People with reflux/sensitive digestion • Children eating many bakery snacks', 'Bicarbonate-based home baking • Yeast fermentation • Simpler bakery methods', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'Sodium carbonates are familiar in baking. Usually low concern, but still part of the processed bakery/additive stack.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0220', 'E501', 'Potassium carbonates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cocoa products • Bakery products • Noodles • Processed foods needing acidity control', 'Hours', 'Gut • Potassium balance', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not limited in normal food-use context', 'Potassium carbonates are alkalising/acidity-regulating agents. They are generally low concern at approved use levels, with awareness mainly around potassium-restricted diets.', '• Adds potassium, usually modestly • Common in alkalised cocoa/technical processing • Product context matters more than the additive alone', '• People on potassium-restricted medical diets • People with sensitive digestion • Children eating many processed bakery/cocoa products', 'Traditional cocoa/bakery methods • Simpler processing • Natural acidity balance', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'Usually low concern, but it tells you the product has been technically adjusted for acidity or processing performance.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0221', 'E503', 'Ammonium carbonates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Cakes • Biscuits • Baking powder • Bakery products • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Ammonia handling', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not limited in normal food-use context', 'Ammonium carbonates are raising agents used in bakery products. They typically decompose during baking, leaving the leavening effect rather than high residual additive levels.', '• Bakery stack with other raising agents • Mainly relevant in biscuits/crackers • Watch with repeated processed bakery intake', '• People with sensitive digestion • Children eating many biscuits/cakes • People avoiding heavily processed bakery foods', 'Yeast/sourdough fermentation • Home baking • Simpler raising systems', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'This is a classic bakery technology additive. It is not a high-risk flag, but it still shows industrial leavening rather than slow traditional preparation.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0222', 'E504', 'Magnesium carbonates', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low/Moderate Awareness', '2/5', '• Powdered foods • Cocoa products • Bakery products • Supplements • Processed foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Magnesium/mineral balance', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not limited in normal food-use context', 'Magnesium carbonates are used as acidity regulators and anti-caking agents. They are generally low concern at normal food additive levels, though higher magnesium intakes can affect digestion.', '• Powder/anti-caking exposure • Adds magnesium, usually modestly • Watch with supplement stacks', '• People with sensitive digestion • People taking magnesium supplements • People with kidney disease should follow clinical advice', 'Better powder storage • Simpler dry mixes • Non-carbonate mineral sources where suitable', 'Approved for permitted uses and levels.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA topic guidance', 'Magnesium carbonates are usually low concern. The Unboxed question is whether the product is a simple food or a powdered/fortified processed item.', '⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/business-guidance/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-08', 'Timeline fields are practical Unboxed guidance, not a medical clearance promise. Scores reflect additive use, likely exposure, stacking and sensitive-user awareness.', TRUE),
