  ('UAL-0262', 'E585', 'Ferrous lactate', 'Others', 'Other technological function', '🟢 Low Awareness', '2/5', 'See authorised food categories', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver', 'Typically within 24–48 hrs*', 'As specified by UK/EFSA where applicable', 'Used within authorised UK limits. Evidence does not indicate concern for the general population when consumed within permitted levels.', 'Consider total daily exposure and other additives in the same product.', 'People with specific allergies or medical dietary advice.', 'Depends on additive function.', 'Approved/additive listed by FSA/GOV.UK; permitted uses and limits depend on food category and legislation.', 'FSA/GOV.UK', 'Look at the whole product rather than a single ingredient.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Source list imported - detail pending', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-05', 'Awaiting detailed EFSA/FSA review.', FALSE),
  ('UAL-0263', 'E620', 'Glutamic acid', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasonings • Instant noodles • Soups and sauces • Meat-flavoured products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'Glutamic acid is an amino acid and umami flavour enhancer. EFSA set a group ADI for glutamic acid and glutamates and noted that exposure may exceed the ADI in some population groups.', '• Belongs with the glutamate group E620–E625 • Umami effect can be boosted by ribonucleotides E627, E631 and E635 • Often appears in salty savoury ultra-processed foods', '• People sensitive to glutamate-rich foods • Children with high savoury snack intake • People tracking salt/flavour-enhancer load', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom powder • Tomato • Parmesan-style savoury ingredients', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is the base of the MSG family. The useful question is how often savoury flavour enhancers are being used to make processed foods more moreish.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA 2017 established group ADI for glutamic acid and glutamates E620–E625. Timeline is practical guidance, not a medical clearance claim.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0264', 'E621', 'Monosodium glutamate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Crisps and savoury snacks • Instant noodles • Seasoning mixes • Soups and sauces • Ready meals', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'MSG is a sodium salt of glutamic acid. EFSA set a group ADI for glutamates; reported short-term symptoms occur in some people, but controlled evidence is mixed and dose-dependent.', '• Often boosted by E627, E631 or E635 • Usually appears in salty savoury products • Can increase palatability and repeated snacking', '• People who report MSG sensitivity • Children with high savoury snack intake • People tracking sodium intake • People monitoring migraine-type triggers', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom powder • Tomato • Herbs and spices • Slow-cooked stock', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'MSG is not automatically the villain it is made out to be, but it is a clear signal to look at the whole savoury snack or ready-meal pattern.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA group ADI applies to glutamic acid and glutamates E620–E625. MSG contributes sodium as well as glutamate.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0265', 'E622', 'Monopotassium glutamate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasonings • Instant noodles • Soups • Processed savoury foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'Monopotassium glutamate is part of the glutamate flavour-enhancer group. EFSA set a group ADI expressed as glutamic acid for E620–E625.', '• Same glutamate exposure group as MSG • May be used with ribonucleotides for stronger savoury flavour • Check repeated savoury processed food intake', '• People sensitive to glutamate-rich foods • People with potassium-restricted medical advice • Children with high snack intake', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom powder • Tomato • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'This is another glutamate salt. The name changes, but the Unboxed check is the same: what else is in the product and how often is it eaten?', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'Group ADI and evidence base taken from EFSA glutamates re-evaluation.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0266', 'E623', 'Calcium diglutamate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury seasonings • Snack foods • Soups and sauces • Processed savoury products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'Calcium diglutamate is one of the authorised glutamate flavour enhancers. EFSA assessed E620–E625 together and set a group ADI.', '• Counts toward total glutamate additive exposure • Umami effect may be boosted by E627/E631/E635 • Usually found in savoury processed foods', '• People sensitive to glutamate-rich foods • Children with frequent savoury snack intake • People tracking additive stacks', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom • Tomato • Onion/garlic-based savoury ingredients', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Treat this as part of the MSG family. The important pattern is savoury flavour stacking, not just one E number.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA group ADI for E620–E625. Additive-specific human symptom evidence remains mixed.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0267', 'E624', 'Monoammonium glutamate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasonings • Soups • Sauces • Processed savoury foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'Monoammonium glutamate belongs to the glutamate flavour-enhancer group. EFSA set a group ADI for glutamic acid and glutamates.', '• Same additive group as MSG • Look out for ribonucleotide boosters • Usually part of a salty savoury formulation', '• People sensitive to glutamate-rich foods • Children with frequent savoury snack intake • People tracking ultra-processed savoury foods', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom powder • Tomato • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'Another member of the glutamate group. It is less common on labels than MSG, but the stacking message is the same.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA 2017 group ADI applies. Timeline is typical amino acid metabolism guidance.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0268', 'E625', 'Magnesium diglutamate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami taste', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snack foods • Seasoning blends • Soups • Sauces • Processed savoury products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', '30 mg/kg body weight/day expressed as glutamic acid', 'Magnesium diglutamate is included in EFSA''s glutamate group assessment. The group ADI is expressed as glutamic acid.', '• Counts toward total glutamate additive exposure • May be combined with E627/E631/E635 • Check salty savoury product patterns', '• People sensitive to glutamate-rich foods • Children with frequent processed snack intake • People tracking flavour-enhancer exposure', 'Yeast extract • Mushroom powder • Tomato • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA', 'The mineral attached to the glutamate is different, but the main label signal is still glutamate-driven savoury enhancement.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2017.4910', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA 2017 group ADI applies to E620–E625.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0269', 'E626', 'Guanylic acid', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Instant noodles • Seasonings • Soups and sauces • Meat-flavoured products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Guanylic acid belongs to the ribonucleotide flavour-enhancer group. These additives are used at low levels to strengthen savoury/umami flavour, often with glutamates.', '• Strongly boosts umami with glutamates • Look out for MSG/E621 and yeast extract • Nucleotide flavour enhancers can make savoury foods more intense', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks • Children with high savoury snack intake', 'Mushroom • Seaweed • Tomato • Slow-cooked stock • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is a flavour amplifier. It is not usually about the dose alone; it is about how it helps processed food taste stronger and harder to stop eating.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA re-evaluation data call exists for E626–E635; JECFA established ADI not specified for disodium 5''-ribonucleotides. Group guidance applied cautiously.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0270', 'E627', 'Disodium guanylate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Crisps • Instant noodles • Seasoning sachets • Soups • Sauces and ready meals', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Disodium guanylate is a nucleotide flavour enhancer. It is commonly used to intensify savoury flavour, especially when combined with glutamates.', '• Often paired with E621 MSG • Works synergistically with inosinates and glutamates • Usually appears in salty savoury snacks and noodles', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking MSG/flavour enhancer stacks • Children with high snack intake', 'Mushroom • Seaweed • Tomato • Herbs and spices • Real stock', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is one of the big “moreish” boosters to recognise on savoury labels, especially when it appears with MSG or E635.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA ADI not specified for related 5''-ribonucleotides; EFSA re-evaluation process/data call noted for E626–E635.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0271', 'E628', 'Dipotassium guanylate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasonings • Instant noodles • Soups and sauces • Processed savoury foods', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Dipotassium guanylate is part of the guanylate/ribonucleotide flavour-enhancer group. It boosts savoury taste at low use levels.', '• Boosts glutamate/umami flavour • Check alongside MSG and inosinate additives • Potassium salt form may matter for people on restricted diets', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People with potassium-restricted medical advice • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks', 'Mushroom • Tomato • Seaweed • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'A less familiar name, but the same pattern: savoury flavour amplification in processed foods.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'Cautious group entry based on ribonucleotide flavour enhancer evidence and regulatory status.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0272', 'E629', 'Calcium guanylate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasoning blends • Soups • Sauces • Meat-flavoured products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Calcium guanylate is a guanylate flavour enhancer used to strengthen savoury taste. It belongs with the ribonucleotide additive group.', '• Look out for MSG/glutamates • Often part of savoury seasoning systems • Works with inosinates and glutamates to boost umami', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking savoury additive stacks • Children with frequent snack intake', 'Mushroom • Tomato • Seaweed • Real stock • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is another flavour booster. It tells you the product has been engineered for a stronger savoury hit.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'Group guidance for ribonucleotide flavour enhancers. Additive-specific EFSA re-evaluation remains limited/pending.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0273', 'E630', 'Inosinic acid', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Instant noodles • Meat-flavoured products • Seasonings • Soups and sauces', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Inosinic acid belongs to the nucleotide flavour-enhancer group and is used to intensify savoury taste, often with glutamates.', '• Boosts MSG/glutamate savoury flavour • Check for combined guanylates and inosinates • Often appears in salty processed foods', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks • Children with high snack intake', 'Meat stock • Mushroom • Tomato • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is a savoury amplifier. It matters most when it appears as part of a flavour-enhancer stack.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA ADI not specified for related ribonucleotides; EFSA data call noted for E626–E635.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0274', 'E631', 'Disodium inosinate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Crisps • Instant noodles • Seasoning sachets • Soups • Ready meals', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Disodium inosinate is a common savoury flavour enhancer. It can strongly boost umami flavour when used with MSG or natural glutamates.', '• Often paired with MSG/E621 • Works with E627 and E635 • Usually appears in salty savoury ultra-processed foods', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking flavour-enhancer exposure • Children with high snack intake', 'Real stock • Mushroom • Tomato • Seaweed • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is one of the label checks for “designed to taste more savoury”. It is about the flavour system, not just one ingredient.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA considered disodium inosinate with disodium guanylate/ribonucleotides and retained ADI not specified.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0275', 'E632', 'Dipotassium inosinate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasonings • Soups • Sauces • Instant noodles', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Dipotassium inosinate is part of the inosinate/ribonucleotide flavour-enhancer group used to strengthen savoury taste.', '• Boosts glutamate flavours • Check with E621, E627 and E635 • Potassium salt form may be relevant for restricted diets', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People with potassium-restricted medical advice • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks', 'Mushroom • Tomato • Real stock • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'Another umami booster. The names vary, but the food pattern is usually the same: salty, savoury, processed and highly palatable.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'Group guidance applied cautiously; EFSA re-evaluation data call noted.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0276', 'E633', 'Calcium inosinate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Instant noodles • Seasonings • Soups and sauces • Meat-flavoured products', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Calcium inosinate is an inosinate flavour enhancer used to intensify savoury flavour, often in combination with glutamates.', '• Works with glutamates and guanylates • Look out for MSG/E621 and E635 • Usually part of a processed savoury seasoning system', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks • Children with frequent snack intake', 'Real stock • Mushroom • Tomato • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is a flavour amplifier more than a stand-alone concern. It teaches you to read the whole seasoning system.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA ADI not specified for related ribonucleotides; EFSA re-evaluation not finalised.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0277', 'E634', 'Calcium 5''-ribonucleotides', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Savoury snacks • Seasoning blends • Instant noodles • Soups • Sauces and ready meals', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA for related ribonucleotides', 'Calcium 5''-ribonucleotides are nucleotide flavour enhancers used to boost savoury/umami taste, often alongside glutamate-rich ingredients.', '• Stronger savoury effect with glutamates • Check MSG/E621, yeast extract and hydrolysed proteins • Usually appears in processed savoury foods', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking flavour-enhancer stacks • Children with high snack intake', 'Mushroom • Tomato • Seaweed • Herbs and spices • Real stock', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is a label clue that flavour has been amplified. It is useful to recognise when processed foods taste unusually intense.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'Related to the E626–E635 ribonucleotide group; EFSA re-evaluation data call and JECFA ADI not specified used as context.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0278', 'E635', 'Disodium 5''-ribonucleotides', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / umami booster', '🟠 Higher Awareness', '4/5', '• Crisps • Instant noodles • Flavoured snacks • Seasoning sachets • Soups and sauces', 'Hours', 'Gut • Normal nucleotide metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', 'ADI not specified by JECFA', 'Disodium 5''-ribonucleotides are a mixture of nucleotide flavour enhancers. JECFA established ADI not specified; EFSA has sought data for re-evaluation of the E626–E635 group.', '• Strong synergy with MSG/glutamates • Can make savoury foods taste much stronger • Look out for E621, yeast extract, hydrolysed proteins and high salt', '• People with gout or uric-acid concerns should seek dietary guidance • People tracking MSG/flavour enhancer stacks • Children with frequent snack/noodle intake', 'Mushroom • Tomato • Seaweed • Real stock • Herbs and spices', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is one of the main “flavour stack” additives. When you see it with MSG, the product has been designed for a stronger savoury hit.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/call/call-data-re-evaluation-ribonucleotides-e-626-635-food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA ADI not specified; EFSA data call indicates re-evaluation work for E626–E635. Higher awareness due to stacking/palatability relevance.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0279', 'E640', 'Glycine and its sodium salt', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / flavour modifier', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Seasonings • Savoury products • Some processed foods • Specialist formulations', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Normal amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'No safety concern at current levels of intake when used as flavouring agent / ADI not specified context', 'Glycine is the simplest amino acid and a normal component of protein. JECFA noted no safety concern at current levels of intake when used as a flavouring agent.', '• Sodium salt may contribute small sodium amounts • Consider supplement intake separately from food additive use • Usually lower concern than savoury enhancer stacks', '• People on sodium-restricted diets • People using high-dose glycine supplements • People with specific medical dietary advice', 'Protein-rich foods • Stock • Gelatine/collagen sources • Simple seasoning', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; JECFA', 'Glycine is an example where the E number is also a normal amino acid. For most people, it is a lower-awareness additive.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://apps.who.int/food-additives-contaminants-jecfa-database/Home/Chemical/5426', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA glycine flavouring evaluation notes no safety concern at current intake levels; additive-specific UK use still governed by authorised categories.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0280', 'E641', 'L-leucine', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / amino acid', '🟢 Low Awareness', '1/5', '• Specialist foods • Powdered products • Supplements • Protein products where used', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Muscle amino acid metabolism', 'Usually within 24 hrs*', 'ADI not specified / not allocated', 'L-leucine is an essential amino acid naturally present in dietary protein. As an additive, it is authorised for specific technological uses, with concern mainly around total supplemental intake rather than normal additive exposure.', '• Supplement intake can be much higher than food additive exposure • Protein powders may contain leucine as a nutrient and/or additive • Look at total amino acid supplementation', '• People using high-dose amino acid supplements • People with kidney or liver medical dietary advice • People on medically supervised protein restrictions', 'Protein foods • Meat • Eggs • Dairy • Beans and pulses', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA/JECFA context', 'Leucine is a normal amino acid, not a classic additive concern. The main thing to separate is food additive use from high-dose supplement use.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://www.efsa.europa.eu/en/topics/topic/food-additives', '2026-07-09', 'Specific EFSA food-additive re-evaluation evidence for E641 is limited in this workbook; entry uses authorised status plus amino acid context.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0281', 'E650', 'Zinc acetate', 'Flavour enhancers', 'Flavour enhancer / flavour modifier', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Chewing gum • Breath-freshening products • Specialist flavour systems • Foods where permitted', 'Hours', 'Gut • Liver • Zinc metabolism', 'Usually within 24–48 hrs*', '0–1 mg/kg body weight/day as zinc (JECFA context)', 'Zinc acetate is a zinc salt used as a flavour modifier. Zinc is an essential mineral, but total zinc intake from fortified foods and supplements matters.', '• Counts toward total zinc exposure • Watch with zinc supplements and fortified foods • Too much zinc can affect copper status over time', '• People taking zinc supplements • Children using fortified products frequently • People with copper deficiency or medical mineral advice', 'Non-zinc flavour systems • Herbs and natural flavouring approaches', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; JECFA', 'This is a mineral-based additive. The concern is not normal label use alone; it is total zinc exposure when supplements and fortified products stack up.', '⭐⭐⭐ Emerging', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://apps.who.int/food-additives-contaminants-jecfa-database/', '2026-07-09', 'JECFA context uses ADI expressed as zinc. Check future EFSA-specific food additive re-evaluation if available.', TRUE),
  ('UAL-0282', 'E900', 'Dimethylpolysiloxane', 'Antifoaming agents', 'Antifoaming agent', '🟡 Moderate Awareness', '3/5', '• Frying oils • Soft drinks in some contexts • Jam and preserves where permitted • Processing aids/anti-foam use', 'Hours', 'Mostly not absorbed • Gut', 'Mostly excreted unchanged in faeces*', '1.5 mg/kg body weight/day', 'EFSA re-evaluated dimethylpolysiloxane and retained the ADI of 1.5 mg/kg bw/day. It is very poorly absorbed and most is excreted unchanged.', '• Often linked to industrial processing or frying systems • Look at fried food frequency and oil quality • More about food context than direct absorption', '• People reducing fried/ultra-processed foods • People tracking additive exposure from takeaway-style foods • People with specific medical dietary advice', 'Better oil management • Mechanical foam control • Shorter processing chains', 'Approved. Use is subject to permitted food categories and limits.', 'FSA/GOV.UK; EFSA; JECFA', 'This is an anti-foam additive, not a nutrient. The bigger Unboxed check is the processed or fried food system it appears in.', '⭐⭐⭐⭐ Moderate', 'Batch detail checked', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/approved-additives-and-e-numbers/approved-additives-and-e-numbers', 'https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/food-additives', 'https://efsa.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.2903/j.efsa.2020.6107', '2026-07-09', 'EFSA 2020 notes very limited gastrointestinal absorption and excretion mostly unchanged in faeces. Timeline adapted accordingly.', TRUE),
